---
title: 'Exploring the LLM Pareto frontier of quality, cost and speed'
---

Stencila Cloud's model router provides you with the "best" model for your input.
It does this by analyzing the outputs of various benchmarking services to
produce normalized scores for quality, speed and cost.
This document describes how that's achieved.

## Data sources

Stencila makes use of publicly-available, open access data sets to evaluate the
models that are available to its users:

| Metric  | Data source                               | Provider                         |
| ------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Quality | Elo rating system                         | Chatbot Arena (previously LMSYS) |
| Speed   | Throughput, measured as tokens per second | Thefastest.ai                    |
| Cost    | Publicly-available pricing data           | LiteLLM                          |


::: table

Model scores of each metric.

| Metric  | Data source                               | Provider                         |
| ------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Quality | Elo rating system                         | Chatbot Arena (previously LMSYS) |
| Speed   | Throughput, measured as tokens per second | Thefastest.ai                    |
| Cost    | Publicly-available pricing data           | LiteLLM                          |

:::

